{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-tannaka-krein-reconstruction","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:tannaka-krein-reconstruction","kind":"proposition","title":"Tannaka--Krein reconstruction of the quantum gauge group","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-braiding-eigenvalue-extraction"],"cites":["references/woronowicz1988","references/deligne1990","references/tannaka1939","references/kassel1995"],"tags":["tannaka-krein","reconstruction","hopf-algebra","fibre-functor"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.tannaka_krein_reconstruction","text":"tannaka-krein-reconstruction.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/tannaka-krein-reconstruction.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:tannaka-krein-reconstruction\"></a><p>By Tannaka--Krein duality, the coend <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H = \\mathrm{End}^{\\otimes}(\\tau) = \\int^{X \\in \\mathbf{C}} \\tau(X)^{\\vee} \\otimes_R \\tau(X)</code> carries a canonical Hopf algebra structure. This provides the monoidal equivalence <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbf{C} \\simeq \\mathrm{Rep}(H)</code>. For generic braiding, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H</code> reconstructs the compact quantum group algebra <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{O}_q(G)</code>. The deformation parameter <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code> is determined by the braiding.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/tannaka-krein-reconstruction.md","leanStatus":"proved","heading":"Proposition","number":"3.7.4"}
